According to the weapons spoiler, Launcher/Missle weapons
don't recieve bonus from strength, while normal throwned weapons
do. I can see why: A bow can only be stretched so far, crossbows
are consistently shot at the same damage.

And when you throw daggers/darts, a main source of damage is
how fast you threw the dart/dagger/star. Strength plays a big role
in that.

But when it comes down to a sling... it can go either way. There
are 2 slings that I'm familiar with, the "Y" sling or slingshot, and
the sling David used vs Golith.

http://www.christiananswers.net/q-abr/slingers2.gif

A good picture of the "David sling". Basically a little cloth that
helps you throw stones (or GEM_CLASS ).

If this is the kind of sling that is in Nethack, then strength
bonus really should apply. There is no limit to the amount
of strength used on this kind of sling like a bow or crossbow.

Mini YANI: Expert slingers vs a Giant has a small chance
of a one hit kill. "You feel like David"

This is the slingshot, which the current sling in nethack works like:
http://www.knightsedge.com/crossbows/ancient-slingshot-4622g.jpg

It is basically a bow for stones; and the lack of strength modifiers
makes a lot of sence.

Considering the fact that cavemen grow into expert slingers,
I'd argue that the more primitive "david" sling is the sling
used :-)

Of course, this makes slings from somewhat ****y weapons
to somewhat average weapons, maybe Cavemen would be a
slightly easier class... Still not the best as daggers and darts
recieve strength bonuses *and* enchantment bonuses, and
darts can be poisoned, but it at least makes the sling considerable
right?

